    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** (73.81) and **Cal Raleigh** (72.86) anchor our lineup as the premier plays. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits immensely from the platoon advantage against Springs, with his elevated position in the two-hole providing massive cumulative upside in Runs and RBI. **Cal Raleigh** remains an elite start, as his power profile against Abbott is bolstered by the catcher\u2019s strong 19% SP skill adjustment and a favorable middle-of-the-order slot. **Daulton Varsho** (69.27) also grades out as a top-tier option, as the combination of an favorable matchup against Martinez and his proven ability to generate production makes him a high-efficiency engine for today\u2019s 5x5 categories.\n\nIn terms of lineup construction, **Luis Arraez** (67.03) and **Taylor Ward** (64.61) provide critical stability at the top of the order. **Taylor Ward** sees a significant boost from his platoon edge against Tolle, while **Luis Arraez** maintains his value through his leadoff spot, effectively insulating his floor against Wacha. The most difficult decision on the bench involved **Tyler Freeman** (51.52), who sat just outside the cut due to his spot in the lower third of the order. While **Tyler Freeman**\u2019s park factors were favorable, the efficiency gap created by the platoon and order advantages possessed by **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Gavin Sheets** made them slightly more attractive options to maximize our game caps.\n\nRisks for the day are minimal but should be monitored. While no severe weather warnings are currently in effect, we are tracking the \"Elite Hold SP\" factor for players like **Masyn Winn**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Daulton Varsho**; their steal efficiency is marginally tempered today by the scouting reports on the opposing batteries. We will continue to evaluate the late-afternoon lineups to ensure that **Yainer Diaz** and **Gleyber Torres** maintain their projected spots, as any shift in the batting order could trigger a re-assessment of their viability against Junk and Taillon, respectively.",
